---
// How AI agents sped up the design work. Hours with AI come from the pi and
// Claude Code session logs (active time, gaps over 10 min dropped). Hours
// without AI are my own estimates. Figures come from the ORLO-Zig public_show/
// folder (deliverables/ai_acceleration/make_diagrams.py, svg-figs skill).
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ShowFigure from '@components/ShowFigure.astro';

const work = [
  { name: 'Simulation core and checks', tasks: 'ZO-1 to ZO-14', ai: 16, est: 160 },
  { name: 'Build-order search', tasks: 'ZO-15 to ZO-22', ai: 7, est: 100 },
  { name: 'Robustness runs, decision package, wheel sizing', tasks: 'ZO-23 to ZO-25, ZO-32', ai: 9.5, est: 140 },
  { name: 'Two and four robots, new parameters', tasks: 'ZO-26 to ZO-37', ai: 7.5, est: 100 },
  { name: 'CAD to Blender, 1 m tiles', tasks: 'ZO-38 to ZO-40', ai: 1.5, est: 60 },
  { name: 'Literature toolkit, 235 papers', tasks: 'ZO-30', ai: 5, est: 80 },
  { name: 'This website and controls code', tasks: '', ai: 7.5, est: 40 },
];
const totAi = work.reduce((s, w) => s + w.ai, 0);
const totEst = work.reduce((s, w) => s + w.est, 0);

// Chart geometry: grouped horizontal bars, one axis (hours).
const AI = '#0287b5';
const EST = '#c2410c';
const max = 160;
const labelW = 0;
const plotW = 380;
const rowH = 58;
const top = 8;
const x = (h: number) => labelW + (h / max) * plotW;
const chartH = top + work.length * rowH + 28;
const ticks = [0, 40, 80, 120, 160];

const accelerated = [
  { what: 'Physics code', how: '6-DOF momentum model, path planner, wheel controller: 134 Python files, 613 tests.' },
  { what: 'Checks', how: 'Conservation gates and analytic cross-checks run on every result, so a bad model fails loudly.' },
  { what: 'Many runs', how: '20 robustness runs and wheel sweeps ran in the background while I did other work.' },
  { what: 'Visuals', how: 'Plots, animations and Blender renders made straight from the saved simulation data.' },
  { what: 'Reading', how: 'Agents searched databases, checked 140 quotes against the PDFs, and wrote paper cards.' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Working with AI"
  description="How AI agents sped up the design work: time with AI against my estimate without it, and how physics simulations set each design decision."
>
  <section class="border-b border-slate-200 bg-gradient-to-b from-arc-50/60 to-white">
    <div class="container-page pt-14 pb-12">
      <p class="eyebrow">Working with AI · Sep to Nov 2026</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 max-w-3xl">How AI agents sped up the design work</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-prose text-lg text-slate-600">
        I set the questions and made the decisions. AI agents wrote and checked the physics code, ran
        the simulations and made the figures. Each design question went from idea to evidence in hours
        instead of weeks.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 grid max-w-3xl grid-cols-2 gap-6 sm:grid-cols-4">
        <div><p class="stat m-0">≈45 h</p><p class="m-0 text-sm text-slate-500">of working sessions, over 9 weeks</p></div>
        <div><p class="stat m-0">≈{totEst} h</p><p class="m-0 text-sm text-slate-500">my estimate without AI</p></div>
        <div><p class="stat m-0">48</p><p class="m-0 text-sm text-slate-500">planned tasks finished</p></div>
        <div><p class="stat m-0">613</p><p class="m-0 text-sm text-slate-500">tests on the physics code</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container-page pt-12 pb-8">
    <article class="article max-w-3xl">
      <section>
        <h2>1. The loop</h2>
        <p>Every study followed the same six steps. The agents did the slow middle; I did the two ends.</p>
        <ShowFigure from="zig" id="ai-workflow" number={1} />
      </section>

      <section class="mt-14">
        <h2>2. Time with AI against without</h2>
        <figure class="my-8">
          <div class="card p-5">
            <div class="mb-4 flex flex-wrap gap-5 text-sm text-slate-600">
              <span class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="inline-block h-3 w-3 rounded-sm" style={`background:${AI}`}></span>With AI (session logs)</span>
              <span class="flex items-center gap-2"><span class="inline-block h-3 w-3 rounded-sm" style={`background:${EST}`}></span>Without AI (my estimate)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-0">
              {work.map((w) => (
                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-1 sm:grid-cols-[14rem_1fr] sm:items-center" style={`min-height:${rowH}px`}>
                  <div class="text-sm leading-5">
                    <span class="font-medium text-slate-800">{w.name}</span>
                    {w.tasks && <span class="block font-mono text-[11px] text-slate-400">{w.tasks}</span>}
                  </div>
                  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${plotW + 60} 40`} class="block w-full" role="img" aria-label={`${w.name}: ${w.ai} h with AI, about ${w.est} h without`}>
                    {ticks.map((t) => <line x1={x(t)} x2={x(t)} y1="0" y2="40" stroke="#e2e8f0" stroke-width="1" />)}
                    <g class="bar">
                      <title>{`${w.name}: ${w.ai} h with AI`}</title>
                      <rect x="0" y="3" width={Math.max(x(w.ai), 4)} height="14" rx="3" fill={AI} />
                      <rect x="0" y="0" width={plotW} height="20" fill="transparent" />
                    </g>
                    <text x={Math.max(x(w.ai), 4) + 6} y="15" font-size="13" fill="#334155">{w.ai} h</text>
                    <g class="bar">
                      <title>{`${w.name}: about ${w.est} h without AI (estimate)`}</title>
                      <rect x="0" y="22" width={x(w.est)} height="14" rx="3" fill={EST} />
                      <rect x="0" y="17" width={plotW} height="17" fill="transparent" />
                    </g>
                    <text x={x(w.est) + 6} y="34" font-size="13" fill="#334155">≈{w.est} h</text>
                  </svg>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
            <div class="hidden sm:grid sm:grid-cols-[14rem_1fr]">
              <span></span>
              <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${plotW + 60} 18`} class="block w-full" aria-hidden="true">
                {ticks.map((t) => <text x={x(t)} y="13" font-size="12" fill="#64748b" text-anchor={t === 0 ? 'start' : 'middle'}>{t} h</text>)}
              </svg>
            </div>
          </div>
          <figcaption class="mt-2.5 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-500">
            <span class="font-semibold text-slate-700">Figure 2. </span>
            Hours with AI are active time in the agent session logs ({totAi} h summed; 45 h of wall-clock
            time, since some agents ran in parallel). Hours without AI are my own estimates for doing the
            same work by hand. The CAD row counts agent session time only.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <details class="mb-6 text-sm text-slate-600">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer text-slate-700">Show as a table</summary>
          <table class="mt-3 w-full border-collapse">
            <thead><tr class="border-b border-slate-300 text-left text-slate-500"><th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Work</th><th class="py-2 pr-4 text-right font-medium">With AI (h)</th><th class="py-2 text-right font-medium">Without AI, est. (h)</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {work.map((w) => <tr class="border-b border-slate-200"><td class="py-2 pr-4">{w.name}</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-right font-mono">{w.ai}</td><td class="py-2 text-right font-mono">{w.est}</td></tr>)}
              <tr class="font-medium text-slate-900"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Total</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-right font-mono">{totAi}</td><td class="py-2 text-right font-mono">{totEst}</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </details>

        <h3>What AI sped up</h3>
        <ul class="mt-3 grid list-none gap-3 p-0 sm:grid-cols-2">
          {accelerated.map((a) => (
            <li class="card p-4 text-sm leading-6">
              <span class="font-semibold text-slate-900">{a.what}.</span> <span class="text-slate-600">{a.how}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-14">
        <h2>3. Physics that set the design</h2>
        <p>
          The model tracks every moving body (robots, gantry, tiles) in free space, where the total
          angular momentum must stay zero. Every run must pass conservation and analytic checks before
          its numbers are used. Each result then fed the next design question.
        </p>
        <ShowFigure from="zig" id="ai-decisions" number={3} />
        <ShowFigure from="zig" id="two-robot-mirror" number={4} />
        <ShowFigure from="zig" id="validation-gap-map" number={5} />
      </section>

      <section class="mt-14">
        <h2>4. From simulation to CAD to render</h2>
        <p>
          The robot CAD from Fusion 360 goes into Blender, driven by the simulated motion and attitude.
          A clearance check found the two robots overlap by up to 104 mm, long before any hardware was
          made. Scaling the design to 1 m tiles meant re-running the same scripts.
        </p>
        <ShowFigure from="zig" id="blender-cad-pair" number={6} />
        <ShowFigure from="zig" id="blender-1m-tiles" number={7} />
      </section>

      <section class="mt-14">
        <h2>5. What stayed with me</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5">
          <li>Choosing the questions, and the test of success for each one.</li>
          <li>Doubting inputs: I asked where the 65 kg frame came from. It was a guess, and replacing it changed the results.</li>
          <li>The design calls, such as the outward spiral for stronger tile joints, which the numbers alone did not pick.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">
          The simulations are verified against physics laws but not yet validated against hardware. See
          the validation gap map above and the Project page for what is not yet known.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .bar:hover rect:first-of-type { opacity: 0.8; }
</style>
